{"kind":"advisory_background","payload":{"affected":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"PyPI","name":"jinja2","purl":"pkg:pypi/jinja2"},"ranges":[{"events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.1.5"}],"repo":"","type":"ECOSYSTEM"}]}],"aliases":["CVE-2024-56326","GHSA-q2x7-8rv6-6q7h"],"details":"An oversight in how the Jinja sandboxed environment detects calls to `str.format` allows an attacker that controls the content of a template to execute arbitrary Python code.

To exploit the vulnerability, an attacker needs to control the content of a template. Whether that is the case depends on the type of application using Jinja. This vulnerability impacts users of applications which execute untrusted templates.

Jinja's sandbox does catch calls to `str.format` and ensures they don't escape the sandbox. However, it's possible to store a reference to a malicious string's `format` method, then pass that to a filter that calls it. No such filters are built-in to Jinja, but could be present through custom filters in an application. After the fix, such indirect calls are also handled by the sandbox.","id":"PYSEC-2026-1475","modified":"2026-07-07T17:24:22.207889Z","published":"2026-07-07T14:34:47.732576Z","references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-56326"},{"type":"FIX","url":"https://github.com/pallets/jinja/commit/48b0687e05a5466a91cd5812d604fa37ad0943b4"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/pallets/jinja"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://pypi.org/project/jinja2"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q2x7-8rv6-6q7h"}],"summary":"Jinja has a sandbox breakout through indirect reference to format method","withdrawn":""},"provenance":{"license_id":"CC-BY-4.0","license_source_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pypa/advisory-database/c4a1fde8cb41b3b5180fed3561596c9ce6de99ad/LICENSE","source_origin":"real_public","source_record_id":"advisory-database-c4a1fde8cb41b3b5180fed3561596c9ce6de99ad/vulns/jinja2/PYSEC-2026-1475.yaml","source_sha256":"4e40288bddd838b87be3b004c721e9384629eaec646c351e8dc8324d53c8195a","source_url":"https://codeload.github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tar.gz/c4a1fde8cb41b3b5180fed3561596c9ce6de99ad"}}

